        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(ui): collapse completed turn work behind a \"Worked for X\" rollup",
        "body": "Closes #105010\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nAfter an agent run finishes, the Control UI chat thread keeps every intermediate step of the turn — tool activity groups and running commentary — at full height. Long runs bury the final answer, and the thread never says how long the run took or gives an at-a-glance done signal.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nOnce a turn reaches terminal state, its intermediate work (tool groups plus assistant commentary ahead of the final reply) now collapses behind one slim disclosure row — a check icon, \"Worked for 2m 52s\", and a chevron — so completed turns read final-output-first while the details stay one click away. Live turns never collapse (in-flight stream runs and, while the run works, the trailing or reply-less turn stay expanded), so the collapse itself doubles as the done indicator. Turns whose tools errored without a recovering reply default to expanded with the existing error styling so failures stay visible. Web Control UI only; the collapse is a render-time pass over the existing chat item pipeline and reuses the activity-group disclosure pattern and per-session expansion store.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCompleted turns in Control UI chat show the user message, one \"Worked for X\" rollup, and the final reply — both in history and the moment a live run finishes. Clicking the rollup expands the full intermediate detail; clicking again re-collapses it. Runs that ended without a reply (aborted, or tool errors) collapse too once the session is idle, with error turns surfacing expanded.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Focused suite on Blacksmith Testbox: `pnpm test ui/src/pages/chat/chat-thread.test.ts` — 86/86 passed (8 new `collapseCompletedTurnWork` tests: collapse shape, duration, live-turn guards, reply-less turns, error flagging, divider boundaries, per-turn independence). Run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29181019400\n- Mock harness (`pnpm dev:ui:mock`) with a new completed work-turn fixture, verified in-browser (toggle both ways, no console errors):\n\n| Collapsed (default) | Expanded |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![collapsed](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/work-rollup/work-rollup-collapsed.png) | ![expanded](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/steipete/openclaw-pr-assets/main/work-rollup/work-rollup-expanded.png) |\n\nNew copy goes through `t()` with keys in `en.ts` only; translations flow through the post-merge locale workflow.\n\n\nNote: the branch also carries the generated locale catch-up produced by the authenticated `control-ui-i18n` sync (the sync fails closed unless every pending key is translated, and `main` had ~976 keys awaiting the post-merge locale-refresh workflow). All bundles pass the keyless drift check with `fallbacks=0`.\n",
        "branch": "claude/collapsible-work-duration-cb7f2e",
